  "interpretation": [
    "Prepared warm measurements exclude import, compilation/JIT, initial host preparation and upload; they include gathering, transforms, fitting, reductions and scalar downloads.",
    "Complete report warm measurements include cleaning, encoding, upload, point/ideal and requested bootstrap refits. End-to-end gains can be much smaller than prepared-kernel gains.",
    "Distance first-call timings are not full process-cold times. Setup/import and some kernel initialization can occur before the first-call timer; use the benchmark tool to measure deployment-specific cold cost.",
    "Small Conditional workloads favor CPU; large and wide classifier cases favor GPU in these measurements. Automatic routing is conservative and explicit device overrides remain available.",
    "FP32 may change strict membership, bins or rarity decisions at rounded boundaries; accuracy reports are workload-specific and do not imply bitwise FP32/FP64 parity.",
